{title: All the Way My Savior Leads Me}
{artist: Fanny J. Crosby / Robert Lowry}
{genre: Hymn, Gospel}
{style: Traditional}
{flow: Meditative}
{key: G}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 4/4}

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[G]All the way my Savior [C]leads me
What have [G]I to ask be[D]side?
Can I [G]doubt His tender [C]mercy
Who through [G]life has been my [D]Guide?
[G]Heavenly peace, di[C]vinest comfort
Here by [G]faith in Him to [D]dwell!
For I [G]know whate'er be[C]fall me
Jesus [G]doeth [D]all things [G]well
For I [G]know whate'er be[C]fall me
Jesus [G]doeth [D]all things [G]well
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[G]All the way my Savior [C]leads me
Cheers each [G]winding path I [D]tread
Gives me [G]grace for every [C]trial
Feeds me [G]with the living [D]bread
Though my [G]weary steps may [C]falter
And my [G]soul athirst may [D]be
Gushing [G]from the Rock be[C]fore me
Lo! a [G]spring of [D]joy I [G]see
Gushing [G]from the Rock be[C]fore me
Lo! a [G]spring of [D]joy I [G]see
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[G]All the way my Savior [C]leads me
O the [G]fullness of His [D]love!
Perfect [G]rest to me is [C]promised
In my [G]Father's house a[D]bove
When my [G]spirit, clothed im[C]mortal
Wings its [G]flight to realms of [D]day
This my [G]song through endless [C]ages
Jesus [G]led me [D]all the [G]way
This my [G]song through endless [C]ages
Jesus [G]led me [D]all the [G]way
{end_of_verse}
